    "title": "Kyle Schwarber Signs New Contract with Phillies",
    "text": "• Kyle Schwarber signed a $150 million, five-year contract with the Philadelphia Phillies.\n• The contract signing occurred just before the expected birth of his daughter.\n• Schwarber rushed to Philadelphia for contract formalities and then returned to Ohio to be with his family.\n• Schwarber will turn 33 in March.\n• He had a season with 56 homers and 132 RBIs.\n• Schwarber expressed his desire to continue contributing to the Phillies and compete for World Series titles.\n• Phillies president Dave Dombrowski emphasized Schwarber's impact on the team.\n• Schwarber won a World Series title with the Cubs in 2016.",
